From b9d8646b162bb9e68969fd215e7799e5c7eecd70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CustomKIMI <customkimi@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:23:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] customkimi: bill every agent of a session in the footer
 cost

The footer priced only the main agent's usage, so foreground, background
and nested subagents were never billed, and a resumed session lost the
subagents it had run before.

A session-scoped billing service keeps each agent's cumulative per-model
usage keyed by agent id and replaces that snapshot on every record instead
of adding it, so no request is counted twice. On first use it restores the
durable usage.record lines of every registered agent (holding a log lease
while reading) and picks up agents registered later; afterwards it
announces every change, including a background subagent that finishes
after the main turn. A malformed usage record or an unreadable journal
hides the cost instead of showing a partial total; a damaged journal is
read up to its last valid line.

The SDK exposes the result as SessionStatus.billingUsage and on a
main-agent status event that still carries the main agent's own snapshot,
so the parent's usage and context meter stay unchanged. The TUI footer
prices billingUsage and falls back to the main agent's usage for engines
that do not report it.

Sums that include a request without a reported cost stay unknown instead
of counting it as free, provider costs must be finite numbers, and the
klient usage schema keeps the cost field.
